# The user manual is built with MkDocs and the Material theme, in CI and by
# `make docs`; nothing here is a project dependency. Every pin is a release at
# least 7 days old: a brand-new release can be missing from some PyPI caches
# for hours, and is when a compromised release is least likely to be noticed.
# Regenerate requirements.txt after changing this file, with a cutoff a week
# before today (Dependabot also proposes updates, with the same cooldown):
#   uv pip compile docs/manual/requirements.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#     --exclude-newer <YYYY-MM-DD one week ago>T00:00:00Z --no-header -o docs/manual/requirements.txt
mkdocs==1.6.1
mkdocs-material==9.7.7
